@startuml component-publishing
' ============================================================
' Component Diagram: Publishing (Approval State Machine)
' CYO Adventure
'
' Source files:
'   src/cyo_adventure/publishing/state_machine.py (Status, Action, Visibility,
'                                                   LEGAL_TRANSITIONS,
'                                                   assert_transition: pure,
'                                                   dependency-free transition table)
'   src/cyo_adventure/publishing/service.py       (submit, auto_reject, approve,
'                                                   send_back, archive, recall:
'                                                   each wraps a transition + ORM
'                                                   writes + record_event, one flush)
'   src/cyo_adventure/publishing/catalog_publish.py (promote_catalog_story():
'                                                   standalone CLI, delegates
'                                                   entirely to service.py's
'                                                   approve(); outside the
'                                                   api/deps.py auth layer;
'                                                   CATALOG_FAMILY_ID scope only,
'                                                   distinct from generation/
'                                                   import_catalog.py, which
'                                                   never publishes)
'   src/cyo_adventure/api/approval.py             (admin-only HTTP surface:
'                                                   submit/approve/send-back/
'                                                   archive/recall/review/
'                                                   review-queue)
'   src/cyo_adventure/publishing/reason_codes.py  (SendBackReasonCodeLiteral +
'                                                   validate_reason_code, and
'                                                   RecallReasonCodeLiteral +
'                                                   validate_recall_reason_code:
'                                                   the two closed vocabularies,
'                                                   moved OUT of api/schemas.py so
'                                                   the domain owns it; the
'                                                   dependency now runs one way,
'                                                   api/schemas.py imports from
'                                                   here. No I/O)
'   src/cyo_adventure/api/review_surface.py       (build_review_surface,
'                                                   build_review_queue_item)
'   src/cyo_adventure/moderation/pipeline.py      (worker-path caller of
'                                                   submit()/auto_reject();
'                                                   see component-moderation.puml)
'   src/cyo_adventure/events/writer.py            (RELEASED, SENT_BACK,
'                                                   STORYBOOK_ARCHIVED,
'                                                   STORYBOOK_RECALLED events)
'   docs/planning/adr/adr-005-mandatory-human-approval.md (amended 2026-06-30:
'                                                   approve/publish is
'                                                   admin-only; no guardian path)
'   docs/planning/tech-spec.md (section: Authorization Matrix)
' ============================================================

skinparam defaultFontName "Roboto"
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam roundCorner 8
skinparam componentStyle uml2

skinparam component {
  BorderColor #555555
  FontColor #222222
}

actor "Admin\n(global safety operator,\ncross-family, ADR-005)" as admin #EDE7F6

component "Moderation Pipeline\nmoderation/pipeline.py\n[worker path]\n[see component-moderation.puml]" as moderation #E8F5E9

package "Publishing" #F3E5F5 {

  component "approval.py [global admin]\napi/approval.py\nPOST .../submit\nPOST .../approve\nPOST .../send-back\nPOST .../archive\nPOST .../recall\nGET .../review\nGET /review-queue" as approval_router #E1BEE7

  component "_load_admin_story()\napi/approval.py\nrequires ctx.principal.is_admin\n(role checked BEFORE any load);\nSELECT ... FOR UPDATE\n(closes #129 concurrency race)" as load_admin #D1C4E9

  component "review_surface.py\napi/review_surface.py\nbuild_review_surface()\nbuild_review_queue_item()\napplies admin noise floor" as review_surface #D1C4E9

  component "State Machine\npublishing/state_machine.py\nassert_transition()\npure, dependency-free" as state_machine #CE93D8

  component "Reason-Code Vocabularies\npublishing/reason_codes.py\nSendBackReasonCodeLiteral\nvalidate_reason_code()\nRecallReasonCodeLiteral\nvalidate_recall_reason_code()\nclosed sets, no I/O" as reason_codes #CE93D8

  component "Publishing Service\npublishing/service.py\nsubmit()\napprove()\nsend_back()\narchive()\nrecall()" as service #CE93D8

  component "auto_reject()\npublishing/service.py\nmachine-side rejection;\nActor.system(), no principal" as auto_reject #CE93D8

  component "Catalog Publish CLI\npublishing/catalog_publish.py\npromote_catalog_story()\nstandalone; outside api/deps.py auth;\nCATALOG_FAMILY_ID scope only" as catalog_publish #CE93D8

}

database "PostgreSQL" as pg #E0F7FA {
  component "Storybook\n.status, .visibility,\n.current_published_version" as storybook_row #E0F7FA
  component "StorybookVersion\n.approved_by, .published_at\n.moderation_report" as version_row #E0F7FA
}

component "Pipeline Event Log\nevents/writer.py [WS-D]\n[see component-events.puml]" as events_log #FFF8E1

' --- HTTP entry ---
admin --> approval_router : "submit / approve /\nsend-back / archive / recall"
approval_router --> load_admin : "admin role check\n(403 before any query)"
load_admin --> storybook_row : "SELECT ... FOR UPDATE"
approval_router --> review_surface : "GET .../review,\nGET /review-queue"
review_surface --> version_row : "blob + moderation_report"

' --- Service / state-machine ---
approval_router ==> service : "submit(session, book)\n[admin path]"
moderation ==> service : "submit(session, book)\n[worker path, post-gate\nclean or repaired]"
moderation ..> auto_reject : "auto_reject(session, book)\n[worker path, hard block]"
service --> state_machine : "assert_transition(\ncurrent, action)"
auto_reject --> state_machine

approval_router ==> service : "approve(session, principal,\nbook, version, visibility)\n[ADMIN ONLY -- ADR-005]"
approval_router --> service : "send_back(session, principal,\nbook, reason, *, reason_code)"
service --> reason_codes : "validate_reason_code(reason_code)\n(in send_back, so the closed set holds\nfor EVERY caller, not only the API)\nvalidate_recall_reason_code(reason_code)\n(same placement, inside recall)"
approval_router --> service : "archive(session,\nprincipal, book)"
approval_router --> service : "recall(session, principal,\nbook, *, reason_code)\n[ADMIN ONLY -- re-checked\nin the service]"

service --> storybook_row : "status, visibility,\ncurrent_published_version"
service --> version_row : "approved_by,\npublished_at"
auto_reject --> storybook_row : "status = needs_revision"

service --> events_log : "RELEASED (approve)\nSENT_BACK (send_back;\npayload {reason_code})\nSTORYBOOK_ARCHIVED (archive)\nSTORYBOOK_RECALLED (recall;\npayload {reason_code})"

note left of reason_codes
  The vocabulary lives here, not in
  api/schemas.py, and the two are easy
  to get backwards. It moved because
  api/schemas.py is what the API
  boundary validates against and what
  the OpenAPI schema is generated from,
  so publishing importing from it while
  it imported the vocabulary would be a
  cycle. api/schemas.py now imports the
  vocabulary FROM here.

  Narrower claim than it looks: this is
  not "the domain never imports from the
  API layer". catalog_publish.py imports
  Principal and Role from api/deps.py at
  runtime, and service.py imports
  Principal from it under TYPE_CHECKING.
  The cycle is the reason, not a rule
  without exceptions.

  The reviewer's free-text `reason` is
  logged and never persisted; only the
  code reaches the event payload (D3).
end note

catalog_publish ==> service : "approve(...)  [standalone CLI path,\nsame approve() as the admin HTTP path]"

note bottom of catalog_publish
  Runs outside the api/deps.py auth
  layer entirely (no HTTP request, no
  session-scoped Principal). Requires
  --approved-by resolving to an admin
  user id, and only Storybooks owned by
  CATALOG_FAMILY_ID are eligible. Kept
  separate from generation/
  import_catalog.py, which imports the
  pre-authored draft-story catalog into
  the review pipeline but never itself
  publishes.
end note

note right of state_machine
  LEGAL_TRANSITIONS (the single source
  of truth for legal hops):

  draft --submit--> in_review
  draft --auto_reject--> needs_revision
  needs_revision --submit--> in_review
  in_review --approve--> published
  in_review --send_back--> needs_revision
  published --archive--> archived
  published --recall--> in_review

  Any other (from_state, action) pair
  raises StateTransitionError -> 409.

  recall (RS-C1) is the only hop that
  moves a book backwards out of a
  reader-facing state without ending its
  life: archived is absorbing, so archive
  was previously published's sole exit.
  It EXTENDS ADR-005 rather than relaxing
  it: a recalled book re-enters in_review
  and needs a fresh admin approval before
  any child sees it again. Emits
  STORYBOOK_RECALLED, whose reason_code
  separates a threshold-driven recall
  from a safety pull.
end note

note right of approval_router
  Every handler in this router is
  admin-only: authorize_family is
  intentionally NOT called (admin
  authority is cross-family, the
  backend safety-review operator).

  approve() is the SOLE code path that
  may set status="published"; it always
  stamps approved_by + published_at in
  the same operation (no-unapproved-
  publish invariant). tech-spec.md's
  Authorization Matrix: guardians get
  403 on approve/publish, including on
  their own family's story -- there is
  no guardian path (ADR-005, amended
  2026-06-30).
end note

note bottom of service
  submit() and approve() both refuse a
  version whose moderation_report is
  still None (BusinessLogicError,
  "cannot submit/approve a version that
  has never been screened by
  moderation"): no unscreened or
  unmoderated version can reach
  in_review or published, regardless of
  which of the two callers (admin HTTP
  path or moderation worker path)
  invokes it.

  approve() additionally runs the WS-G
  series-chain validation gate for a
  series book before publishing (legacy
  pre-WS-G chains are grandfathered and
  skip the check).
end note

@enduml
